function rgbToHsv(r, g, b) {
  r /= 255;
  g /= 255;
  b /= 255;

  const max = Math.max(r, g, b);
  const min = Math.min(r, g, b);
  const c = max - min;

  let h = 0;
  if (c === 0) {
    h = 0;
  } else if (max === r) {
    h = (g - b) / c;
  } else if (max === g) {
    h = 2 + (b - r) / c;
  } else if (max === b) {
    h = 4 + (r - g) / c;
  }

  h = h * 60;
  if (h < 0) {
    h += 360;
  }

  const s = c / max;
  const v = max;

  return [h, s, v];
}
```
This function takes three arguments, `r`, `g`, and `b`, which represent the red, green, and blue components of the RGB color, respectively. It returns an array containing the hue, saturation, and value (HSV) components of the color.

The function first normalizes the RGB values to the range [0, 1] by dividing them by 255. It then calculates the maximum and minimum values of the RGB components, and the chroma (difference between the maximum and minimum values) using the formula `c = max - min`.

Next, the function calculates the hue using the formula `h = (g - b) / c` if the maximum value is red, `h = 2 + (b - r) / c` if the maximum value is green, and `h = 4 + (r - g) / c` if the maximum value is blue. The hue is then scaled to the range [0, 360] by multiplying it by 60.

Finally, the function calculates the saturation and value using the formulas `s = c / max` and `v = max`, respectively.

